Role/Tools.pm:633-643 (and Chat.pm _tool_loop_iteration ~l.330 + simple_chat_with_tools_f ~l.435) read the raw body via parse_response, never chat_response, so the k301/k311/k317 error guards do not run. A 200 with {"error":{...}}, a choice with finish_reason error + error object, choices:[] or Gemini promptFeedback.blockReason yields no tool calls -> response_text_content -> the loop RETURNS an empty string as the final answer.

Repro (offline, MockAsyncHTTP): body {"error":{"message":"upstream overloaded","code":502}} -> chat_with_tools_f returns ""; chat_f on the same body dies "response carried an error: upstream overloaded (502)". Same for finish_reason error, choices:[], Gemini {promptFeedback:{blockReason:SAFETY}}.

Fix: after parse_response in all three loops, run the same body-error checks chat_response runs (factor them out of the dialect chat_response into a helper callable on raw $data, e.g. $self->_croak_on_body_error($data)), then continue with response_tool_calls. Regression test per dialect (openai, gemini, anthropic, responses) in t/6x.
